changed.

The Swin Transformer backbone in swin.py originates with Microsoft
(https://github.com/microsoft/Swin-Transformer, MIT), and reaches this package
through BiRefNet's own copy of it.

refine_foreground() in image.py is a blur-fusion foreground estimator from
Photoroom (https://github.com/Photoroom/fast-foreground-estimation), credited in
upstream's handler.py and reproduced here with the same two-pass radii.

The model weights are licensed separately from this code, and identically: every
checkpoint mozo publishes carries "license: mit" on its ungated model card. The
training data behind some of them includes datasets published under their own,
in some cases research-only, terms (for example P3M-10k and AM-2k). mozo takes
the publisher's MIT grant on the weights as stated and does not track the terms
of the data behind them; PROVENANCE.md records where the chain stops.
